explanation:
INSERT INTO ... SELECT can populate a table from query results. This complete independent example copies distinct ID/name pairs.
```sql
CREATE TABLE raw_items(category_id INTEGER,category_name TEXT);
CREATE TABLE categories(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,name TEXT);
INSERT INTO raw_items VALUES(10,'paper'),(10,'paper'),(20,'tools');
INSERT INTO categories(id,name)
SELECT DISTINCT category_id,category_name
FROM raw_items;
SELECT id,name
FROM categories
ORDER BY id;
```
The result is 10/paper and 20/tools; the repeated source pair becomes one category.

